# Online Retail Sales Dashboard (Power BI)

An interactive **Power BI dashboard** built to analyze transactional sales data from a UK-based online retail store. The report — titled **"TATA Online Retail Data Set"** on the dashboard itself — visualizes revenue trends, country-wise performance, and customer activity from over 540,000 invoice line items spanning a full year of sales.

## 📖 About the Project

This project takes a raw e-commerce transaction dataset and turns it into a single, focused Power BI report page that highlights key sales patterns at a glance. The dataset captures real invoice-level transactions — including order details, product descriptions, quantities, prices, customer IDs, and countries — from **December 2010 to December 2011**.

The dashboard was built to answer a few core business questions:
- How is revenue trending month over month?
- Which countries generate the most sales?
- How active are customers, and how does that relate to revenue?
- Where in the world are orders coming from?

## 📊 Dataset Overview

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| Source file | `Online_Retail.xlsx` |
| Total rows | 541,909 transaction line items |
| Date range | December 1, 2010 – December 9, 2011 |
| Unique customers | 4,372 |
| Unique products | 4,070 |
| Countries represented | 38 |
| Primary market | United Kingdom (~91% of orders) |

**Columns in the dataset:**
- `InvoiceNo` — Unique invoice/order number
- `StockCode` — Product/item code
- `Description` — Product name
- `Quantity` — Units purchased per line item
- `InvoiceDate` — Date and time of the transaction
- `UnitPrice` — Price per unit
- `CustomerID` — Unique customer identifier
- `Country` — Customer's country

> Note: Some rows have a missing `CustomerID` (guest/unregistered orders), and a small number of rows have negative quantities, which typically represent cancelled orders or returns.

## 📈 Dashboard Contents

The Power BI report (`TATA.pbix`) consists of a single report page with the following visuals:

- **Revenue Trend (Line Chart)** — Monthly revenue plotted over the order date's Date Hierarchy, showing how sales performed across the year.
- **Year Slicer** — An interactive filter allowing the report to be sliced by year for focused analysis.
- **Revenue by Country (Bar Chart)** — A clustered bar chart comparing revenue across countries, with order quantity shown in tooltips.
- **Customer Activity vs. Revenue (Bar Chart)** — A clustered bar chart relating customer counts to revenue figures.
- **Country Map (Filled Map)** — A geographic visualization showing average order quantity by country.
- **Title Banner** — A textbox header labeling the report.

All visuals are connected to a single data table (**"Online Retail"**) loaded from the Excel source, making the report fully interactive — filtering on the year slicer or clicking into a country updates every visual on the page.

## 🛠️ Built With

- **Microsoft Power BI Desktop** — report building, data modeling, and visualization
- **Microsoft Excel** — source data format (`.xlsx`)

## 📁 Files

- `TATA.pbix` — The Power BI report file (includes the data model and report visuals)
- `Online_Retail.xlsx` — The source dataset used to build the report

## 🚀 How to Open

1. Install **Power BI Desktop** (free, available from Microsoft)
2. Open `TATA.pbix` directly — the dataset is already embedded in the file's internal data model, so no separate data connection setup is required
3. Use the year slicer and visual interactions to explore the data

## 🎯 Project Goals

- Practice transforming raw transactional data into a clear, business-relevant dashboard
- Build experience with Power BI's core visual types: line charts, bar charts, slicers, and maps
- Explore sales trends, geographic distribution, and customer activity from a real-world style dataset
- Strengthen data modeling and report design skills using Power BI Desktop

